# Build artifacts
dist/
build/

# ...except the Go package called `build`, which is source and not an artifact.
#
# `build/` above matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so it swallowed
# `backend/internal/build/` — the one variable every command reads to say which
# build it came from. The package compiled here and did not exist in the
# repository, so CI failed at `go vet` in one second with "no required module
# provides package .../internal/build" while everything passed locally. A
# .gitignore rule that hides source is invisible exactly to the person who
# wrote the source.
#
# The directory is re-included rather than the file: git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so un-ignoring a file inside one does nothing.
!backend/internal/build/

# Local tool config (personal, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json
.serena/project.local.yml
.serena/cache/

# Serena runtime output (config and memories ARE committed)
.serena/cache/
.serena/logs/

# Tauri POS
pos/node_modules/
pos/dist/
pos/src-tauri/target/

# Regenerated by the Tauri build from tauri.conf.json and the capability files,
# so committing them only produces churn on every plugin or version bump.
pos/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# TypeScript incremental build cache. Machine-local, rewritten by every
# build, and was tracked by accident — it turned up as a change in every
# commit that happened to run one.
*.tsbuildinfo
zatca-docs/

# Screenshots the visual pass writes. Output of a check, not source.
/.shots/
/shots/

# Throwaway SQL validation harness; not part of the product.
backend/sqlcheck/

# 21st.dev CLI install record. Pins the same skills that ARE committed under
# .claude/skills/, but writes absolute machine paths and install timestamps
# into it, so committing it produces a diff on every machine that reinstalls.
/.21st/
